-- title:
--   Cusp-regular integral level-M' functions lie in the j-chart
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$, a nonzero natural number $M'$ with $q \nmid M'$, and a prime $\ell_g$ with $\ell_g \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ and $\ell_g \mid M'$. Let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}} =$ `AlgebraicClosure ℚ` lying over $q$, meaning $q$ is a nonunit of $A$; let $W$ be a finset of places of `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'` whose members are exactly the supersingular places `ssPlaces q M'` (rational places, affine geometric, with value of the generic $j$-function in the supersingular set), let $s$ be an element of $W$, and assume `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` $\le$ `fieldBar q M'`, the base change to $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ of the function field of $X_H(q^2M')$ for $H =$ `levelH q M'`. Let $R_0$ be a constant reduction of $A$ on `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` with values in `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'`, assumed compatible with coefficientwise reduction: for every Laurent series $y$ over $A$ whose coefficientwise image lies in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'`, that image lies in $R_0$`.integers` and its $R_0$-residue, read as a Laurent series over the residue field of $A$, is the coefficientwise reduction of $y$. Further data: an intermediate field $k_0$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q}$ and $\pi_0 \in k_0$ lying in $A$, such that $A_0 := A \cap k_0$ is a discrete valuation ring with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$, is Henselian, and has algebraically closed residue field, together with the approximation hypothesis that every element of $A$ differs from some element of $k_0 \cap A$ by an element of the maximal ideal of $A$; a primitive $(q\ell_g)$-th root of unity $\xi \in k_0$ admitting a ring homomorphism $k_0 \to \mathbb{C}$ sending $\xi$ to $e^{2\pi i/(q\ell_g)}$; the subgroup $H_1 =$ `levelH q M'` $\cap \ker\big((\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/\ell_g)^\times\big)$; the field $K =$ `laurentBaseChange k₀ (xHFunctionField (q^2*M') H₁)`, an $A_0$-algebra compatibly with $k_0$; and a nonzero $j \in K$ whose underlying Laurent series is `coeffEmb k₀ jq`. Finally let $gf$ be a Laurent series over $\mathbb{Q}$ lying in `modularFunctionFieldFull M'` whose image in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` lies in $R_0$`.integers` and which is cusp-regular, in the sense that every place $P$ of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $\operatorname{ord}_P(jq) \ge 0$ also satisfies $\operatorname{ord}_P(gf) \ge 0$, and assume `coeffEmb k₀ gf` $\in K$. The conclusion is that this element of $K$ lies in `chartAlgFin A₀ K j`, that is, it is integral over the $A_0$-subalgebra of $K$ generated by $j$.
--
--   This is the base case of the integrality analysis for the $j$-finite chart of the integral model of $X_{H_1}(q^2M')$ over $A_0$: a rational modular function of level $M'$ which is $R_0$-integral and has no poles away from the cusps of the $j$-line is integral over $A_0[j]$. It feeds the auxiliary-level results on rigid charts and Galois invariants used in the level-lowering argument.
-- source:
